# =============================================================================
# LOCAL SUPABASE (Docker) — you do NOT need a Supabase Cloud project yet
# =============================================================================
#
# What runs where:
# - `npm run local:supabase` starts Docker containers: Postgres, Auth, REST,
#   Realtime, Storage, Studio, etc. (the Supabase CLI manages compose for you.)
# - Your Next app uses the URL + anon key below to talk to that local stack.
#
# You do NOT need:
# - A hosted "project ref" (the random id in the dashboard URL)
# - A https://xxxxx.supabase.co URL
# - `supabase link` (only when you push migrations to a hosted project)
#
# The name `project_id = "olive-marketing"` in supabase/config.toml is only a
# local label (Docker volume/network name). It is not your cloud project id.
#
# Quick start:
#   1. Install & open Docker Desktop (engine must be running).
#   2. cp .env.example .env.local
#   3. npm run local:supabase    # first run downloads images; can take a few minutes
#   4. npm run dev
#
# Dashboard (Studio): http://127.0.0.1:54323
# If anything fails, run: npm run supabase:status
#
# =============================================================================

# Public site URL (no trailing slash) — used for canonical URLs, sitemap, RSS, JSON-LD, OG.
# Local: http://localhost:3000   Production: https://your-domain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Facebook: optional override of the URL stored in Supabase (`site_contact`, editable under Admin → Site contact).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FACEBOOK_URL=https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61587077835514

# Facebook Pixel & Conversions API (CAPI)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FB_PIXEL_ID=              # Pixel ID (public, used client-side)
# FB_PIXEL_ID=                          # Same Pixel ID (server-side, used by CAPI)
# FB_ACCESS_TOKEN=                      # Conversions API access token (server-side only)

# Optional: after someone submits the lead form, show “Pick a time on the calendar” (Cal.com, Calendly, etc.)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAL_BOOKING_URL=https://cal.com/your-org/intro

# Hero: full-bleed background video (MP4). Unset = built-in CC0 placeholder loop; set your own CDN URL for production.
# Use poster / none / false / 0 to show the poster image only (no video).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_VIDEO_URL=https://your-cdn.com/hero-loop.mp4
# Optional poster frame while the video loads (defaults to built-in image if unset)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_POSTER_URL=https://...

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0

# Local service role — same for every CLI "supabase start" stack; dev/server only, never ship to browsers.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6InNlcnZpY2Vfcm9sZSIsImV4cCI6MTk4MzgxMjk5Nn0.EGIM96RAZ35RFHNBQGlnfNHIu9SzKbLK8ygBV3o9OOk

# =============================================================================
# HOSTED SUPABASE (when you deploy) — then you get a real project + keys
# =============================================================================
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...   # Project Settings → API → anon public

# =============================================================================
# Docker image for Next.js only (optional) — build-args must match hosted URL/keys
# =============================================================================
# docker build \
#   --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="$NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL" \
#   --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="$NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY" \
#   -t olive-marketing .
